      "projects": [
        {
          "title": "Big Data Processing with Hadoop",
          "subtitle": "Mar 2020 - Apr 2020",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "•\tImplemented a simple word count program using MapReduce on 3 text files stored in HDFS.\n•\tGenerated the top 10 occurring tri-grams in the input files by replacing the keywords in the input with '$' using MapReduce program. A global mapper was created to take the output of all local reducers which was then passed to a global reducer that combined the tri-grams and incremented their counts.\n•\tCreated an inverted index of all the words occurring in the input files using MapReduce. Words and the corresponding list of filenames in which they appear was given as the output.\n•\tPerformed a relational join on 2 text files using MapReduce. The input text files were joined on the primary key constraint.\n•\tImplemented the K-nearest neighbor algorithm using MapReduce of Hadoop. The mapper program was used to output the distances and the labels associated with them to the reducer which in turn sorted the distances according to the K-neighbors and predicted their class label. \n\nLanguage used: Python \nFrameworks used: Hadoop\n"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Implementation of Predictive Analytics",
          "subtitle": "Feb 2020 - Feb 2020",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "•\tImplemented Principal Components Analysis(Dimensionality Reduction), K-Nearest Neighbors and  K-means clustering models from scratch using Numpy and Pandas.\n•\tUsing Bagging and Bootstrap aggregration, developed multiple decision tree classifiers and implemented Random Forest classification from scratch.\n•\tDeveloped Ensemble Model using K-NN, Support Vector Machine(SVM), Decision Tree and Logistic Regression models  and implemented the voting classifier on them that gave 97% accuracy in classification of data using scikit-learn.\n•\tPerformed GridSearch on SVM, K-NN and Decision Tree models to tune their hyperparameters and output optimal hyperparameters with 95% accuracy.\n\nLanguage used: Python 3\nFrameworks used: Tensorflow\n"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Implementation of end-to-end search engine for analyzing Twitter Data",
          "subtitle": "Nov 2019 - Nov 2019",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "•\tBuilt an end-to-end solution for searching tweets which involved content ingestion, topic categorization and sentiment analysis. Statistical information of the results obtained was presented in graphical and chart formats.\n•\tCrawled and effectively indexed over 400K multilingual tweets using Apache Solr in EC2 instance of AWS for analyzing the impact of political rhetoric in traditional and social media.\n\nFrameworks used: PyFlask, Bootstrap, Apache Solr,AWS"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Binary Classification Model using Logistic Regression",
          "subtitle": "Oct 2019 - Oct 2019",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "•\tImplemented the binary classification on the Wisconsin Diagnostic Breast Cancer (WDBC) dataset using logistic regression as a classifier to distinguish each cell into 2 classes by comparing them with 30 features given in dataset.\n•\tTrained the classifier to classify tumour cells as benign or malignant with 98.2% accuracy and  93.3% precision.\n\nLanguage used: Python \nFrameworks used: Numpy, Pandas"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Multiclass Classification Model using Neural Network",
          "subtitle": "Sep 2019 - Sep 2019",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": " •\tImplemented single hidden layer neural network on Fashion-MNIST dataset consisting of 70K images, classifying each 28X28 grayscale image and mapping it to its best  matched label associated with 10 classes from scratch.\n•\tExecuted multilayer neural network with 87.3% and Convolutional neural network(CNN) with 88% accuracy using Keras and Tensorflow.\n\nLanguage used-Python "
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Evaluation of Information Retrieval Models",
